 dict(pmid='', doi='10.1016/j.atmosenv.2026.122510', journal='Atmospheric Environment', title='Long term trends in air pollutants over major cities of India', tier='C', basis='Reference / regulatory monitor', short='Long-term trends in air pollutants over major Indian cities (metadata only)', design='Metadata only: no abstract in Crossref at issue time', pm='Long-term air pollutant records over major Indian cities (per title); species not specified', geo='India (major cities)', endpoint='Long-term pollutant trends (per title)', affil='not stated; not stated', n="Metadata only. The title indicates an analysis of long-term trends in air pollutants over major cities of India (Atmospheric Environment), from a group at Aryabhatta Research Institute and PRL by author listing. No abstract reached the index at issue time, so no finding is asserted. Relevance: India's regulatory network has expanded rapidly and unevenly, so trend estimates depend heavily on which stations enter when; the same station-availability problem governs whether low-cost networks can extend such series backwards. Recheck for the station set and trend method when indexed.", sub=corpus.EXPO),
 dict(pmid='', doi='10.1016/j.apr.2026.103291', journal='Atmospheric Pollution Research', title='Real-world particle-bound PAH emissions from inland diesel sightseeing vessels: Impacts of diesel particulate filter retrofit', tier='C', basis='Lab / research instrument', short='Real-world particle-bound PAH emissions from inland diesel sightseeing vessels with and without diesel particulate filter retrofit (metadata only)', design='Metadata only: no abstract in Crossref at issue time', pm='Real-world particle-bound PAH emissions, DPF-retrofitted vs unretrofitted diesel vessels (per title)', geo='Taiwan', endpoint='Particle-bound PAH emission factors and DPF retrofit effect (per title)', affil='not stated; not stated', n='Metadata only. The title indicates real-world measurement of particle-bound PAH emissions from inland diesel sightseeing vessels and the effect of diesel particulate filter retrofit (Atmospheric Pollution Research). No abstract reached the index at issue time, so no finding is asserted. Relevance: retrofit evaluation on working vessels is exactly the setting where regulatory monitoring is absent and portable or on-board instruments carry the measurement; particle-bound PAH also marks the toxic fraction that mass-only sensors cannot distinguish. Recheck for emission factors and retrofit efficiency when indexed.', sub=corpus.OCC),
 dict(pmid='', doi='10.1016/j.apr.2026.103290', journal='Atmospheric Pollution Research', title='Temporal Variability of Atmospheric Fine Particles in Tehran, Iran', tier='C', basis='Reference / regulatory monitor', short='Temporal variability of atmospheric fine particles in Tehran (metadata only)', design='Metadata only: no abstract in Crossref at issue time', pm='Atmospheric fine particle concentrations in Tehran (per title); averaging period not stated', geo='Iran (Tehran)', endpoint='Temporal variability of fine particles (per title)', affil='not stated; not stated', n='Metadata only. The title indicates an analysis of the temporal variability of atmospheric fine particles in Tehran, Iran (Atmospheric Pollution Research). No abstract reached the index at issue time, so no finding is asserted. Relevance: Tehran combines basin meteorology, dust intrusion and dense traffic, so hour-to-hour variability is large and a handful of reference stations under-represent it; this is the kind of record that sets the variance a sensor network would have to resolve. Recheck for the monitoring period, station count and whether dust events are separated when indexed.', sub=corpus.EXPO),
 dict(pmid='', doi='10.1007/s44408-026-00181-8', journal='Aerosol and Air Quality Research', title='Spatiotemporal Variations of Smoke Haze in a Mountain-Valley Region of Northern Thailand Based on Microsensors and Day-Night Remote Sensing', tier='C', basis='Low-cost sensor / network', short='Smoke haze in a northern Thailand mountain-valley region mapped from microsensors plus day-night remote sensing (metadata only)', design='Metadata only: no abstract in Crossref at issue time', pm='Microsensor PM network combined with day-night satellite remote sensing (per title)', geo='Thailand (northern mountain-valley region)', endpoint='Spatiotemporal variation of smoke haze (per title)', affil='not stated; not stated', n='Metadata only. The title indicates spatiotemporal analysis of smoke haze in a mountain-valley region of northern Thailand based on microsensors and day-night remote sensing (Aerosol and Air Quality Research, National Central University author listing). No abstract reached the index at issue time, so no finding is asserted. Relevance: direct - a low-cost sensor network fused with satellite retrievals in complex terrain during biomass-burning season is the deployment pattern this digest tracks, and the open questions are co-location, humidity correction and whether night-time retrievals add anything over the sensors. Priority recheck when indexed.', sub=corpus.SENS),
